; LIMIT 03: a function works on one list element type, so every list helper
; and every sort is rewritten for each type that needs it.
;
; cons, head, tail, and is_empty work on any list, but a def cannot: its
; parameter types are fixed. The prelude's rev, push, append, and length are
; all (list int) only. And a sort cannot take its ordering as an argument
; (no function values, LIMIT 02), so it is rewritten for each ordering too.
;
; What it cost in these programs, all duplicates of code that already exists
; for (list int) or would be one generic sort:
;
;   wordfreq  rev_wc_onto, Halves, deal, merge, sort_wc (33 lines)
;   calc      rev_toks (4 lines)
;
; about 37 of the 485 lines of wordfreq and calc outside their tests, none of
; it hard, all of it the place a copy drifts from its original. The smallest
; program, and what tools/l0check says about it:
;
;   03-no-generic-functions.l0:24:11: error: argument 1 of rev must be (list int), but this is (list Pair)

(data Pair (Pair (list int) int))

(def main () int
  (let ps (rev (cons (Pair "a" 1) (cons (Pair "b" 2) (nil Pair))))
    0))
